{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>The blessing, if you obey etc. and the curse, if you do not obey.</b> A parable: an old man sitting at the crossroads, with two paths before him. One begins with thorns and ends in a level plain, and one begins in a level plain and ends with thorns. He warns those passing by there and says to them: Beware of this one that begins in a level plain, for it is entirely thorns to its very end; go on this one that begins with thorns, for its end is a level plain. Whoever listens to him, even though he struggles a little at the beginning, afterward walks in peace. But whoever does not listen to him and goes on that one that begins in a level plain — stumbles at the end. So too a person who commits a transgression and follows his own willful desire finds satisfaction and a straight path in this world, and when he falls and dies, he goes to Gehenna, which is entirely thorns. But one who labors in this world and toils in Torah and commandments inherits the World to Come, which is entirely a level plain, with satisfaction and joy."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:52.019548183Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}